1
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:03,702
Good morning, listeners.

2
00:00:03,652 --> 00:00:07,280
Today is October 06, 2026.

3
00:00:07,280 --> 00:00:15,466
Overnight, Wall Street delivered a split tape as the Nasdaq jumped over one percent to record highs while long duration bond yields surged.

4
00:00:15,466 --> 00:00:21,300
The Standard and Poor 500 climbed fifty-one points, closing near seventy-eight hundred.

5
00:00:21,300 --> 00:00:29,829
The Nasdaq Composite led the rally, adding two hundred eighty-six points to hit an all-time high of twenty-seven thousand five hundred forty-four.

6
00:00:29,829 --> 00:00:35,540
The Dow Jones Industrial Average lagged, edging up just zero point one eight percent.

7
00:00:35,540 --> 00:00:39,388
The divergence across rates defines this market regime.

8
00:00:39,388 --> 00:00:44,179
The ten-year Treasury yield surged back to five point three five percent.

9
00:00:44,179 --> 00:00:48,628
The thirty-year bond yield broke above five point seven percent.

10
00:00:48,628 --> 00:00:55,724
In contrast, the two-year yield eased after soft consumer inflation data removed October rate hike bets.

11
00:00:55,724 --> 00:00:59,363
Shorter yields support rich growth equity multiples.

12
00:00:59,363 --> 00:01:05,331
However, long-end yields reflect heavy federal deficit issuance and term premium pressures.

13
00:01:05,331 --> 00:01:14,228
Global oil bounced after sabotage reports on Saudi east-west pipelines, but settled back as baseline crude flows continued uninterrupted.

14
00:01:14,228 --> 00:01:19,204
Beneath the headline index records lies an extreme divergence in market breadth.

15
00:01:19,204 --> 00:01:24,657
Capital flows into index funds have reached one point nine trillion dollars this year.

16
00:01:24,657 --> 00:01:30,736
Forty cents of every passive index dollar flows straight into the top ten mega-cap tech stocks.

17
00:01:30,736 --> 00:01:35,711
The S and P equal-weighted index has fallen for seven consecutive weeks.

18
00:01:35,711 --> 00:01:43,738
That seven-week losing streak has happened only twice before: during the 2002 dot-com bust and the 2022 bear market.

19
00:01:43,738 --> 00:01:48,934
Over half of Russell three thousand stocks sit twenty percent below their highs.

20
00:01:48,934 --> 00:01:57,206
Bulls point to washed-out retail sentiment, arguing passive institutional liquidity will trigger an aggressive short squeeze toward eight thousand.

21
00:01:57,206 --> 00:02:04,572
Bears counter that market concentration leaves indexes vulnerable to a trap if bond auctions push yields higher this week.

22
00:02:04,572 --> 00:02:11,667
Tech capital expenditure cycles continue to branch outward from core semiconductors into critical physical bottlenecks.

23
00:02:11,667 --> 00:02:20,405
In chip fabrication, Elon Musk confirmed discussions with Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing Company regarding TerraFab foundry operations.

24
00:02:20,405 --> 00:02:26,741
The news sent TSMC to fresh record highs, while Intel slipped on fears of order dilution.

25
00:02:26,741 --> 00:02:33,542
Simultaneously, power constraints have made utilities the newest artificial intelligence infrastructure play.

26
00:02:33,542 --> 00:02:41,385
Vistra Energy advanced three percent after the United States government announced a four-billion-dollar loan program for nuclear facilities.

27
00:02:41,385 --> 00:02:46,814
Vistra reclaimed its fifty-day moving average, signaling accelerating momentum.

28
00:02:46,814 --> 00:02:57,243
In enterprise artificial intelligence, Meta Platforms gained after deploying its Muse agent platform, with independent merchants on Shopify integrating directly into the system.

29
00:02:57,243 --> 00:03:03,701
In custom compute, Cerebras surged nine percent following direct endorsements from OpenAI leadership.

30
00:03:03,701 --> 00:03:09,572
Meanwhile, a parallel infrastructure trade is accelerating across computational biology.

31
00:03:09,572 --> 00:03:16,520
The artificial intelligence drug discovery sector is replicating the historic semiconductor supply chain rotation.

32
00:03:16,520 --> 00:03:30,233
Capital is rotating out of binary biotech drug trials into physical bottlenecks like Twist Bioscience for DNA synthesis, Recursion Pharmaceuticals for robotic laboratories, and Schrodinger for molecular simulation software.

33
00:03:30,233 --> 00:03:35,282
Three individual equities demand immediate risk management focus this morning.

34
00:03:35,282 --> 00:03:37,537
First, Nvidia.

35
00:03:37,537 --> 00:03:43,579
Consensus models forecast upcoming quarterly revenues expanding seventy percent year over year.

36
00:03:43,579 --> 00:03:49,645
Management is preparing an unprecedented two-hundred-thirty-five-billion-dollar share repurchase program.

37
00:03:49,645 --> 00:03:57,844
Nvidia shares are breaking out toward a six-trillion-dollar market capitalization, corresponding to two hundred forty-nine dollars per share.

38
00:03:57,844 --> 00:04:04,523
Yet forward price-to-earnings ratios sit at seventeen times, well below historical tech bubble peaks.

39
00:04:04,523 --> 00:04:12,121
Immediate technical resistance sits at two hundred fifty dollars, with initial support anchored at two hundred thirty-five dollars.

40
00:04:12,248 --> 00:04:14,722
Second, SpaceX.

41
00:04:14,672 --> 00:04:23,998
The newly renamed SpaceX Superintelligence entity crossed a two-point-two-trillion-dollar valuation following sixteen percent gains over two trading sessions.

42
00:04:23,998 --> 00:04:29,329
Shares settled at two hundred thirty-eight dollars and ninety cents against heavy trading volume.

43
00:04:29,329 --> 00:04:34,219
Morgan Stanley holds an overweight rating with a three-hundred-dollar price target.

44
00:04:34,219 --> 00:04:42,687
The key operational catalyst remains Starship Flight Fifteen, testing simultaneous launch tower recovery of booster and spacecraft.

45
00:04:42,687 --> 00:04:47,233
Traders should watch the two hundred dollar mark as strong structural support.

46
00:04:47,233 --> 00:04:49,562
Third, McDonald's.

47
00:04:49,562 --> 00:04:57,049
Shares trade around two hundred thirty-three dollars, down thirty percent from all-time highs of three hundred thirty-five dollars.

48
00:04:57,049 --> 00:05:06,130
Consumer resistance to price increases has compressed traffic, but earnings remain resilient across five consecutive quarters of positive revenue growth.

49
00:05:06,130 --> 00:05:15,444
McDonald's trades at seventeen times forward earnings with a three point three percent dividend yield backed by forty-nine consecutive years of dividend increases.

50
00:05:15,444 --> 00:05:24,182
Tactical buyers are positioning initial tranches at two hundred thirty dollars, reserving secondary risk allocation at the two hundred ten dollar floor.

51
00:05:24,182 --> 00:05:28,986
Conversely, consumer discretionary weakness remains acute elsewhere.

52
00:05:28,986 --> 00:05:40,616
Nike continues to bleed toward thirty-three dollars after guided sales declines of high single digits, while European luxury titans Hermes and Louis Vuitton trade near ten-year valuation troughs.

53
00:05:40,616 --> 00:05:44,623
That concludes today's XiaoFang Finance Morning Brief.

54
00:05:44,623 --> 00:05:48,790
Thank you for listening, trade safely, and see you tomorrow.
